 "briefing": {
  "situation": "A-day, 20 October 1944. The Leyte landings are under way and the transports lie off the beaches. You launch from Essex with two wingmen, thirteen and a half miles seaward of the landing area. A Japanese raid of bombers and fighters is inbound. Keep the transports afloat until the raid is gone, then land aboard Essex.",
  "loadout": "clean"
 },
 "history": {
  "text": "On 20 October 1944 U.S. Sixth Army landed on the east coast of Leyte, north at Palo and Tacloban and south at Dulag, under a partly cloudy to cloudy sky, with carrier aircraft overhead. This mission is a historical composite: the raid, its strength and the sortie are authored for the game, not a reconstruction of one recorded attack. The beach, the transports and the landing craft are representative of the assault, not a count of it.",
  "sources": [
   "U.S. Army, Leyte: The Return to the Philippines, ch. V (landing date and beach sectors): https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/USA/USA-P-Return/USA-P-Return-5.html",
   "U.S. Navy aerology report, The Assault Landings on Leyte Island (A-day weather): https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/USN/rep/NAVAER/Leyte/index.html"
  ]
 }
